&lt;p&gt;I&apos;m running Python 2.7.13&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In order to run the tool I have changed the file locally but I&apos;m not an expert of Python so I will not submit a patch&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16024009" author="sijie@apache.org" created="Thu, 25 May 2017 01:36:21 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=eolivelli&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;eolivelli&quot;&gt;eolivelli&lt;/a&gt; I think this is fixed, right?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16026246" author="eolivelli" created="Fri, 26 May 2017 12:53:23 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Yes it is OK now.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I noticed that GitHub does not give access to user emails of other users anymore.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If I use my own Oauth token my email as &quot;reviewer&quot; is returned.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I wonder If we can drop the reviewer email from commit messages (actually I am often rewriting the message dropping the &amp;lt;None&amp;gt; strings)&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16026503" author="sijie@apache.org" created="Fri, 26 May 2017 16:56:53 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I believe you need to make your email public.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
